(A thing's map field passed to a value parameter is copied into it: the
 field grows by its own name and the parameter keeps what it was given.)
A thing called ledger has
  a map called counts.

a ledger called shop.
Set shop's counts's "apples" to 1.

To 'look' with a value called kept.
    For each step from 1 to 40, Set shop's counts's "{step}" to step.
    Print "kept: {kept}".

'look' of shop's counts.
Print "the shop counts {shop's counts's length} things".
